FUNDING STRATEGY
Option 1: Bootstrap (Not Realistic)
•	$850K is too much for most founders to self-fund
•	Would require significant personal wealth or loans
Option 2: Friends & Family Round
•	Raise $200K - $300K to build MVP (Months 1-4)
•	Then raise Seed round based on traction
Option 3: Pre-Seed / Seed Round (Recommended)
•	Target Raise: $1.5M - $2M
•	Use of Funds:
o	$850K - $1.2M for Year 1 operations (as detailed above)
o	$300K - $500K for Year 2 runway extension
o	$200K - $300K buffer for unexpected costs
•	Valuation: $5M - $8M pre-money (typical for pre-seed stage)
•	Equity Given: 20-30%
Option 4: Accelerator (Y Combinator, Techstars)
•	YC provides $500K for 7% equity + 3 months of mentorship
•	Great for first-time founders
•	ChowPal fits YC's thesis (marketplace, social, international)
 
