FINAL RECOMMENDATIONS
✅ DO:
1.	Hire slow, fire fast - Quality over speed in team building
2.	Negotiate volume discounts - AWS, CDN providers give 20-30% off at scale
3.	Use equity creatively - Offer 0.5-1.5% to early employees to reduce cash burn
4.	Track burn rate weekly - Know exactly where money is going
5.	Build buffer - Raise 30% more than you think you need
❌ DON'T:
1.	Hire too fast - Each person costs $85K-$120K loaded (salary + benefits + tools)
2.	Overbuild infrastructure - Start lean, scale when needed
3.	Spend on vanity metrics - No fancy office, expensive conferences, etc.
4.	Underprice talent - Cheap engineers cost more in bugs and delays
5.	Ignore compliance - FERPA violations can kill the company
 
